WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:00:24.729 --> 00:00:27.011
Previously on
Strange New Worlds...

3
00:00:27.036 --> 00:00:29.463
All I ever wanted since
I first saw the stars

4
00:00:29.488 --> 00:00:31.185
was to join Starfleet.

5
00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.696
I'm an Illyrian. I've
committed a Federation offense.

6
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.314
If you shelter me they
could come after you. too.

7
00:00:36.339 --> 00:00:37.745
I welcome that discussion.

8
00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.358
I'm arresting
Commander Una Chin-Riley

9
00:00:39.382 --> 00:00:41.064
for violations of
our anti-genetic

10
00:00:41.089 --> 00:00:42.229
modification directive.

11
00:00:42.254 --> 00:00:43.865
I didn't ask for this job.

12
00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.052
- You need a lawyer.
- She won't respond.

13
00:00:46.077 --> 00:00:47.419
She won't take my calls either.

14
00:00:47.444 --> 00:00:48.924
This is not a plum case.

15
00:00:48.949 --> 00:00:50.789
I'm gonna talk to her
myself. face-to-face.

16
00:00:50.814 --> 00:00:52.322
Just hang in there. Number One.

17
00:00:52.347 --> 00:00:54.436
That's an order. Pike out.

18
00:00:59.485 --> 00:01:01.028
She needs a hospital.

19
00:01:01.052 --> 00:01:02.725
That
is out of the question.

20
00:01:02.749 --> 00:01:05.273
- Her leg isn't healing.
- It will.

21
00:01:05.317 --> 00:01:07.754
It's going
to get infected.

22
00:01:07.798 --> 00:01:09.645
If we go into the
hospital. they might see her

23
00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:12.628
fighting infection. They'll
run tests to find out.

24
00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.761
- Mom?
- I know. baby.

25
00:01:14.805 --> 00:01:17.545
I know it hurts.

26
00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:19.244
You're gonna be okay.

27
00:01:19.269 --> 00:01:21.576
I promise.

28
00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:24.118
It needs to get set
or it won't heal.

29
00:01:24.162 --> 00:01:25.511
Her system can't handle it.

30
00:01:25.554 --> 00:01:28.035
She is a child.
She needs a doctor.

31
00:01:28.079 --> 00:01:31.517
Look. if we go to the
hospital now. they'll see.

32
00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.301
and we'll lose everything.

33
00:01:33.345 --> 00:01:35.183
Her life will be
ruined. all of ours.

34
00:01:35.643 --> 00:01:38.829
We'll figure this
out. She'll be okay.

35
00:01:38.854 --> 00:01:41.727
Una will be okay.

36
00:01:42.789 --> 00:01:44.791
Starfleet would
like to offer a deal.

37
00:01:44.816 --> 00:01:47.522
Plead guilty to knowingly
submitting false information

38
00:01:47.547 --> 00:01:49.288
to Starfleet by
failing to disclose

39
00:01:49.313 --> 00:01:51.533
your genetic
modification status.

40
00:01:51.755 --> 00:01:53.844
and we'll accept
dishonorable dismissal.

41
00:01:53.887 --> 00:01:56.150
No prison time.

42
00:01:56.194 --> 00:01:58.586
Dishonorable dismissal?

43
00:01:58.611 --> 00:02:01.783
No exile. You'll still be
a free Federation citizen.

44
00:02:01.808 --> 00:02:03.431
Starfleet is willing
to seal your records

45
00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:04.610
and look the other way.

46
00:02:04.635 --> 00:02:06.420
They want to cover
their mistake.

47
00:02:06.445 --> 00:02:08.746
They are grateful
for your service.

48
00:02:08.771 --> 00:02:10.904
Una. you don't want
to drag this out.

49
00:02:10.948 --> 00:02:12.950
And you don't want
others to get dragged in.

50
00:02:12.993 --> 00:02:15.138
It's a fair deal.

51
00:02:15.163 --> 00:02:16.996
It's a good deal.
given the evidence.

52
00:02:17.041 --> 00:02:19.882
She's right. We
won't get better.

53
00:02:19.907 --> 00:02:21.576
This charge can carry
two years imprisonment

54
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.777
at the minimum.

55
00:02:23.917 --> 00:02:27.399
Don't you think we should
sidebar this conversation?

56
00:02:28.493 --> 00:02:29.624
That's a good idea.

57
00:02:29.894 --> 00:02:31.316
Take some time.

58
00:02:31.359 --> 00:02:32.839
talk it over with your counsel.

59
00:02:32.864 --> 00:02:35.953
How can he counsel me
when he works for you?

60
00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:48.337
Captain's personal
log. star date 2393.8.

61
00:02:48.362 --> 00:02:50.486
I have traveled to
the Vaultera Nebula

62
00:02:50.511 --> 00:02:52.878
to find legal help
for my first officer.

63
00:02:52.903 --> 00:02:56.297
The atmosphere here is not
suitable for human life.

64
00:02:56.341 --> 00:02:59.779
The locals. however.
have adapted.

65
00:02:59.804 --> 00:03:02.241
Yes. he's still here.

66
00:03:02.266 --> 00:03:04.442
Yes. I told him.

67
00:03:04.523 --> 00:03:07.265
No. he did not.

68
00:03:07.308 --> 00:03:09.202
Okay.

69
00:03:11.225 --> 00:03:14.794
- Counselor Ketoul still can't see you today.
- I can wait.

70
00:03:14.838 --> 00:03:16.535
I told you she's booked.

71
00:03:16.578 --> 00:03:20.060
She has a deposition.
then an arraignment.

72
00:03:20.104 --> 00:03:21.409
I can wait.

73
00:03:26.414 --> 00:03:29.026
I don't think that you can.

74
00:03:30.027 --> 00:03:31.158
Try me.

75
00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:44.606
Fine.
fine. fine. Okay!

76
00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:47.347
Ugh!

77
00:03:49.887 --> 00:03:52.720
You can take off your mask. Mr. Pike.

78
00:03:52.745 --> 00:03:54.844
The air is safe for you now.

79
00:03:58.536 --> 00:03:59.929
I knew you were stubborn.

80
00:03:59.954 --> 00:04:01.772
I just didn't think
you were stupid.

81
00:04:01.797 --> 00:04:04.475
This planet is
inhospitable to all but...

82
00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:05.980
Except to Illyrians.

83
00:04:06.193 --> 00:04:10.178
Genetically engineered
to survive in this...

84
00:04:10.203 --> 00:04:11.690
charming environment.

85
00:04:11.715 --> 00:04:13.875
You would think that would
allow us a measure of privacy.

86
00:04:13.899 --> 00:04:15.278
Should have returned my calls.

87
00:04:15.303 --> 00:04:16.957
And you should learn
to take a hint.

88
00:04:16.982 --> 00:04:19.224
Or do they not teach reading
the room at the Academy?

89
00:04:19.249 --> 00:04:20.585
Been a while since I
was at the Academy.

90
00:04:20.609 --> 00:04:22.655
so I don't recall.

91
00:04:25.385 --> 00:04:26.865
Una needs your help.

92
00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:28.974
Starfleet Command found
out that she's Illyrian.

93
00:04:28.999 --> 00:04:31.262
It was only a matter of
time before she was outed.

94
00:04:31.305 --> 00:04:34.352
Starfleet will never let an
Illyrian serve. Not openly.

95
00:04:34.395 --> 00:04:37.746
But that is not my
problem. Mr. Pike.

96
00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:40.040
Now. I really do
have a busy day.

97
00:04:40.065 --> 00:04:41.893
Neera.

98
00:04:41.918 --> 00:04:43.798
I don't know what
happened between you two.

99
00:04:43.823 --> 00:04:45.486
but she's your friend.

100
00:04:45.511 --> 00:04:48.688
Una Chin-Riley is not my
friend. and neither are you.

101
00:04:48.713 --> 00:04:51.847
- Please leave.
- I know why you feel the way you do about Starfleet.

102
00:04:51.872 --> 00:04:53.699
the Federation. all of us.

103
00:04:53.724 --> 00:04:54.976
I saw some things.

104
00:04:55.001 --> 00:04:57.655
On a research mission to an
abandoned Illyrian colony.

105
00:04:57.679 --> 00:05:01.553
we found out that it
wasn't so... abandoned.

106
00:05:01.596 --> 00:05:03.360
I saw what can
happen to Illyrians

107
00:05:03.385 --> 00:05:05.073
who reverse their
genetic modification

108
00:05:05.098 --> 00:05:08.138
just so the Federation
will accept them.

109
00:05:09.213 --> 00:05:11.476
Old fears can be
hard to let go of.

110
00:05:11.519 --> 00:05:15.088
but we were wrong about
Illyrians. All of us.

111
00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.005
I was wrong.

112
00:05:19.049 --> 00:05:22.139
Congratulations. You
discovered empathy.

113
00:05:22.182 --> 00:05:25.229
Let me know when the rest of
your Federation catches up.

114
00:05:27.971 --> 00:05:29.973
They're going to dismiss her.

115
00:05:30.791 --> 00:05:33.160
Everything she's strived
for. her life's work.

116
00:05:33.185 --> 00:05:34.795
her entire career.

117
00:05:34.838 --> 00:05:37.014
Everything that
she's contributed.

118
00:05:37.039 --> 00:05:40.434
Dishonorable dismissal
is getting off easy.

119
00:05:40.461 --> 00:05:43.024
Starfleet race
laws are draconian.

120
00:05:43.049 --> 00:05:45.182
She's lucky she isn't getting
charged with sedition.

121
00:05:47.164 --> 00:05:50.906
Yes. Mr. Pike. I am
familiar with her case.

122
00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.178
The proceedings are sealed.

123
00:05:53.203 --> 00:05:54.901
I make it my business
to know what happens

124
00:05:54.926 --> 00:05:56.583
behind closed doors.

125
00:05:56.608 --> 00:05:59.350
Many of my clients'
lives depend on it.

126
00:05:59.393 --> 00:06:02.831
Now. if that will be all.

127
00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:08.881
How's that working out for you?

128
00:06:08.924 --> 00:06:11.405
- The cases against the Federation.
- Excuse me?

129
00:06:11.449 --> 00:06:13.233
See. I do my homework. too.

130
00:06:13.277 --> 00:06:15.325
Ten cases thrown
out or overturned

131
00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.430
in two years for
insufficient evidence?

132
00:06:17.455 --> 00:06:19.805
Good cases. too. as
far as I can tell.

133
00:06:21.198 --> 00:06:22.850
Take this case.

134
00:06:22.895 --> 00:06:25.419
If you win. half the
quadrant will know it.

135
00:06:25.463 --> 00:06:27.548
And it'll bring your other
cases more attention.

136
00:06:27.573 --> 00:06:29.270
Maybe the attention
that they deserve.

137
00:06:29.313 --> 00:06:31.551
Are you attempting to
bribe me. Mr. Pike?

138
00:06:31.576 --> 00:06:33.620
I'm trying to convince you.

139
00:06:34.907 --> 00:06:36.848
I'm trying to save
an old friend.

140
00:06:36.879 --> 00:06:38.177
And maybe do some good here.

141
00:06:38.215 --> 00:06:39.887
Are you? Or are you gonna

142
00:06:39.912 --> 00:06:41.324
let whatever happened
between you and Una

143
00:06:41.348 --> 00:06:43.350
get in the way of
your life's work?

144
00:06:44.569 --> 00:06:47.093
Just take a look
at the case file.

145
00:06:47.137 --> 00:06:49.139
You?

146
00:06:49.182 --> 00:06:51.184
I doubt you'd even
break a sweat.

147
00:06:52.185 --> 00:06:54.144
You're a piece of work. Pike.

148
00:06:54.476 --> 00:06:56.320
Yeah.

149
00:06:56.345 --> 00:06:58.426
But you still haven't said no.

150
00:07:05.981 --> 00:07:08.245
Visitor.

151
00:07:08.288 --> 00:07:09.289
Neera!

152
00:07:09.333 --> 00:07:11.683
I had to see it for myself.

153
00:07:11.726 --> 00:07:13.999
I said this would happen.

154
00:07:14.294 --> 00:07:16.383
After 25 years. the
first thing you say to me

155
00:07:16.427 --> 00:07:17.655
is "I told you so"?

156
00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:19.633
I didn't think you'd...

157
00:07:19.658 --> 00:07:21.939
I'm not here for a reunion.

158
00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:24.216
Tell me the story of the story.

159
00:07:24.241 --> 00:07:25.894
Short version. your words.

160
00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:32.834
Until two months ago.
my record with Starfleet

161
00:07:32.878 --> 00:07:33.880
was spotless.

162
00:07:33.905 --> 00:07:35.378
When they didn't know.
they didn't care.

163
00:07:35.402 --> 00:07:36.795
The only thing that's changed

164
00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:38.735
is that they know the truth.

165
00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:40.718
And that you lied about it.

166
00:07:42.038 --> 00:07:43.865
Must be nice.

167
00:07:44.487 --> 00:07:45.405
What's that?

168
00:07:45.456 --> 00:07:48.051
It's just. some Illyrians
have modifications

169
00:07:48.076 --> 00:07:51.427
they can't hide. and
some of us refuse to.

170
00:07:51.551 --> 00:07:52.900
Neera. I should have...

171
00:07:52.925 --> 00:07:55.014
Please proceed. Commander.

172
00:07:56.322 --> 00:07:58.019
So then somebody turned me in.

173
00:07:58.044 --> 00:08:00.555
and now Starfleet is
asking me to hide again.

174
00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.012
so that no one has to know

175
00:08:02.037 --> 00:08:04.823
an Illyrian climbed
the ranks of Starfleet.

176
00:08:04.848 --> 00:08:07.547
It'll be like it never happened.

177
00:08:07.608 --> 00:08:10.176
- Like I never happened.
- So?

178
00:08:10.201 --> 00:08:12.203
You had your playtime.
acting like one of them.

179
00:08:12.228 --> 00:08:16.232
Accept your dismissal. take
your licks and go home.

180
00:08:16.259 --> 00:08:17.434
No.

181
00:08:17.459 --> 00:08:18.939
Why not?

182
00:08:18.964 --> 00:08:21.924
Because I shouldn't
have to hide anymore.

183
00:08:21.984 --> 00:08:23.377
None of us should.

184
00:08:23.494 --> 00:08:25.713
I know I should
have done better.

185
00:08:25.757 --> 00:08:27.975
I didn't stand up
when I should have.

186
00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.065
I'm standing up now.

187
00:08:31.458 --> 00:08:34.113
I'll tell opposing counsel
their deal is rejected.

188
00:08:34.157 --> 00:08:35.767
Thank you.

189
00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:38.371
Don't. I'm not
doing this for you.

190
00:08:38.396 --> 00:08:40.050
I'm doing this for me.

191
00:08:40.075 --> 00:08:42.973
And for all the Illyrians
who can't or just won't

192
00:08:42.998 --> 00:08:46.227
pretend to not be who
they really are...

193
00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:48.134
so they can run
away to Starfleet.

194
00:08:55.482 --> 00:08:56.962
Una rejected my deal.

195
00:08:56.987 --> 00:08:58.206
Good.

196
00:08:59.573 --> 00:09:02.402
Do you know how hard it was
to get that deal approved?

197
00:09:02.446 --> 00:09:03.534
I called in every favor.

198
00:09:03.577 --> 00:09:04.883
And do you think that was easy?

199
00:09:04.926 --> 00:09:06.206
Because I can tell
you it was not.

200
00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:07.215
Maybe you should have
thought about that

201
00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:08.232
before arresting her.

202
00:09:08.257 --> 00:09:10.005
Don't be
a child. Chris.

203
00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:11.478
I know you think I betrayed you.

204
00:09:11.503 --> 00:09:13.485
Una should be on my bridge
right now doing her job.

205
00:09:13.509 --> 00:09:15.130
not sitting in some jail cell.

206
00:09:15.155 --> 00:09:18.334
I don't write the code.
and my job... our job...

207
00:09:18.359 --> 00:09:19.447
Oh. our job.

208
00:09:19.472 --> 00:09:21.247
Is to uphold it. regardless.

209
00:09:21.291 --> 00:09:22.949
Una broke the law.

210
00:09:22.974 --> 00:09:25.107
And what if the law is wrong?

211
00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:32.784
Chris. I didn't ask to
be put on this case.

212
00:09:32.867 --> 00:09:35.348
If you stop and
look for one second.

213
00:09:35.392 --> 00:09:37.016
you'll see I've done
everything in my power

214
00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:38.564
to help Una.

215
00:09:38.589 --> 00:09:40.765
That plea deal
was her best shot.

216
00:09:40.812 --> 00:09:42.466
And now that she's
turned it down.

217
00:09:42.491 --> 00:09:44.102
my boss. the judge
advocate general.

218
00:09:44.127 --> 00:09:45.389
is looking into the case.

219
00:09:45.414 --> 00:09:47.803
I don't know why. but
whatever the reason.

220
00:09:47.828 --> 00:09:49.685
it won't be good for Una.

221
00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:51.930
She should have taken the deal.

222
00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:58.284
See you in court.

223
00:10:09.339 --> 00:10:10.992
We'll begin
the arraignment

224
00:10:11.036 --> 00:10:13.081
as soon as the
prosecution arrives.

225
00:10:13.125 --> 00:10:16.495
Ah. What's this?

226
00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:18.174
Vice Admiral Pasalk.

227
00:10:18.274 --> 00:10:20.276
I didn't know you
were joining us today.

228
00:10:23.282 --> 00:10:24.718
Admiral. in light
of the defense's

229
00:10:24.743 --> 00:10:26.279
rejection of a plea bargain.

230
00:10:26.304 --> 00:10:28.698
We would like to petition the
court to amend the charges

231
00:10:28.723 --> 00:10:30.725
against Lieutenant
Commander Chin-Riley.

232
00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:34.058
You may proceed. Captain Batel.

233
00:10:34.083 --> 00:10:36.689
For failure to disclose
her genetic modification status.

234
00:10:36.714 --> 00:10:39.636
we are charging Una Chin-Riley
with knowingly submitting

235
00:10:39.661 --> 00:10:41.458
false information to Starfleet

236
00:10:41.483 --> 00:10:45.139
as well as violating
Starfleet code 614 to 617

237
00:10:45.164 --> 00:10:47.297
prohibiting Starfleet
officers from engaging in

238
00:10:47.322 --> 00:10:48.714
permanent bioengineering.

239
00:10:48.739 --> 00:10:51.132
and two counts of sedition.

240
00:10:53.948 --> 00:10:56.386
We're seeking dishonorable
dismissal and 20 years

241
00:10:56.411 --> 00:10:58.108
in a Federation penal colony.

242
00:11:06.526 --> 00:11:08.398
Space.

243
00:11:09.747 --> 00:11:11.966
The final frontier.

244
00:11:13.794 --> 00:11:17.320
These are the voyages of
the starship Enterprise.

245
00:11:18.538 --> 00:11:21.367
Its five-year mission:

246
00:11:21.411 --> 00:11:24.414
to explore strange new worlds..

247
00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:29.114
To seek out new life

248
00:11:29.157 --> 00:11:32.726
and new civilizations.

249
00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:36.861
to boldly go where no
one has gone before.

250
00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:55.823
Twenty years for lying
on an application?

251
00:12:55.848 --> 00:12:58.647
You decided to fight back and
not make this easy for them.

252
00:12:58.672 --> 00:13:01.119
They want to
make an example out of you.

253
00:13:01.144 --> 00:13:03.930
- What do we do?
- We fight.

254
00:13:05.187 --> 00:13:06.615
Who's first on
their witness list?

255
00:13:06.646 --> 00:13:08.973
Admiral Robert April.

256
00:13:08.998 --> 00:13:10.846
April sponsored my
application to the Academy.

257
00:13:10.871 --> 00:13:12.802
I served under him for
years and he promoted me.

258
00:13:12.826 --> 00:13:14.349
- This is good for us. no?
- No.

259
00:13:14.374 --> 00:13:15.941
Pasalk wouldn't bring
a friendly witness

260
00:13:15.966 --> 00:13:17.228
without a strategy.

261
00:13:17.253 --> 00:13:19.211
Put me on the stand.

262
00:13:19.236 --> 00:13:20.890
Let them see that
being an Illyrian

263
00:13:20.915 --> 00:13:23.159
doesn't change who
I am as an officer.

264
00:13:23.184 --> 00:13:26.530
Are you being funny?
You were never funny.

265
00:13:26.555 --> 00:13:28.143
I know it's normally
not a good idea.

266
00:13:28.168 --> 00:13:30.625
but shouldn't they see me. a
successful Starfleet officer?

267
00:13:30.650 --> 00:13:31.806
It's a good story.

268
00:13:31.831 --> 00:13:35.037
Your story doesn't
matter to their case.

269
00:13:35.062 --> 00:13:37.021
You broke the law.
I put you up there.

270
00:13:37.046 --> 00:13:39.048
they'll just use you to
corroborate their facts.

271
00:13:39.073 --> 00:13:41.031
Or worse. to tear you
down. or likely bring down

272
00:13:41.056 --> 00:13:42.836
a bunch of your so-called
friends with you.

273
00:13:45.816 --> 00:13:47.513
Do you care about my story?

274
00:13:47.557 --> 00:13:50.630
I care that my client

275
00:13:50.655 --> 00:13:53.266
not hand the
prosecution the case.

276
00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:57.082
My way this time. Una.

277
00:14:00.918 --> 00:14:02.615
Your way.

278
00:14:06.395 --> 00:14:09.093
The captain suggested you
could set up shop here.

279
00:14:11.776 --> 00:14:13.734
I bet he did.

280
00:14:14.341 --> 00:14:16.779
Well. she's not using it.

281
00:14:21.524 --> 00:14:23.482
I'll need access
to the Starfleet

282
00:14:23.507 --> 00:14:25.676
Uniform Code of Justice.

283
00:14:25.701 --> 00:14:28.268
I assume it's in your database.

284
00:14:28.293 --> 00:14:30.991
Also. Una's service records.

285
00:14:33.516 --> 00:14:35.822
Thank you. Lieutenant
Noonien-Singh.

286
00:14:40.386 --> 00:14:42.432
Is there something else?

287
00:14:42.457 --> 00:14:44.651
I think I might be of some
assistance to the case.

288
00:14:44.676 --> 00:14:48.212
Counselor. are you familiar
with Starfleet v. Wyck?

289
00:14:48.237 --> 00:14:50.892
I am a civil rights lawyer.

290
00:14:51.017 --> 00:14:53.106
Yes. of course.

291
00:14:53.231 --> 00:14:56.451
If I understand the principle
behind the ruling. then...

292
00:14:56.495 --> 00:14:59.629
Starfleet v. Wyck is
used as an example of

293
00:14:59.672 --> 00:15:01.718
"fruit of the poisonous tree."

294
00:15:01.743 --> 00:15:04.447
If evidence is procured
through illegal means.

295
00:15:04.472 --> 00:15:06.088
it's inadmissible in court.

296
00:15:06.113 --> 00:15:08.594
You think some of the
evidence against Una

297
00:15:08.619 --> 00:15:10.011
was illegally obtained?

298
00:15:10.036 --> 00:15:11.433
If it was. could you
get her case thrown out

299
00:15:11.457 --> 00:15:12.791
on a technicality?

300
00:15:12.816 --> 00:15:15.079
If the evidence was rotten.

301
00:15:15.122 --> 00:15:17.908
I might be able to get
her case dismissed.

302
00:15:17.951 --> 00:15:20.693
Lieutenant. is there something
you know that I should know?

303
00:15:20.718 --> 00:15:23.459
Just let me cover
all the bases first.

304
00:15:23.522 --> 00:15:26.873
Well. you know where I'll be.

305
00:15:38.537 --> 00:15:40.017
May I?

306
00:15:41.466 --> 00:15:43.082
Fraternizing with the enemy?

307
00:15:43.486 --> 00:15:45.689
I'll take my chances.

308
00:15:46.715 --> 00:15:47.846
You look awful.

309
00:15:47.871 --> 00:15:49.461
Thanks for that.

310
00:15:49.486 --> 00:15:51.041
Does this have something
to do with the fact that

311
00:15:51.065 --> 00:15:53.180
your name wasn't on the
witness list for the defense?

312
00:15:53.204 --> 00:15:54.334
I know what you're gonna say.

313
00:15:54.358 --> 00:15:56.270
Putting me on the witness
stand is a terrible idea.

314
00:15:56.294 --> 00:15:58.358
But you want to fight
for your friend.

315
00:15:58.383 --> 00:16:00.123
And I can handle it.

316
00:16:00.345 --> 00:16:02.826
I've served with Una longer
than anyone else on this crew.

317
00:16:02.851 --> 00:16:05.201
I'm in the best position
to speak to her character.

318
00:16:05.226 --> 00:16:06.619
When did you two meet?

319
00:16:06.826 --> 00:16:10.134
Uh. I gave a speech
to her Academy class

320
00:16:10.177 --> 00:16:11.657
forever ago.

321
00:16:11.701 --> 00:16:13.909
That must
have been awful for you.

322
00:16:13.934 --> 00:16:16.153
I know how you hate to give
long. inspiring speeches.

323
00:16:17.697 --> 00:16:21.193
I was speaking about a
test mission I'd flown.

324
00:16:22.059 --> 00:16:24.888
Una came up to me afterward
and. uh. pointed out

325
00:16:24.931 --> 00:16:27.586
- a mistake I'd made during reentry.
- Bold.

326
00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:29.632
And annoying.

327
00:16:29.675 --> 00:16:31.677
But she was right.

328
00:16:31.721 --> 00:16:34.549
She had the guts to tell me.

329
00:16:34.593 --> 00:16:36.682
April once told me that
every good captain needs

330
00:16:36.726 --> 00:16:38.771
a first officer who will
tell him when he's wrong.

331
00:16:38.815 --> 00:16:42.166
Yeah. he said that
to me once. too.

332
00:16:43.602 --> 00:16:46.131
And when did you first
learn that she was Illyrian.

333
00:16:46.156 --> 00:16:47.277
Captain Pike?

334
00:16:49.652 --> 00:16:53.960
I ask again. How
long were you aware

335
00:16:53.985 --> 00:16:56.161
that you were harboring
an Illyrian on your ship.

336
00:16:56.186 --> 00:16:57.710
Captain?

337
00:16:57.735 --> 00:16:59.911
I will remind you
you are on the stand.

338
00:16:59.936 --> 00:17:02.219
and under oath you do not have
the option of not answering.

339
00:17:02.243 --> 00:17:04.376
All right. you've
made your point.

340
00:17:04.401 --> 00:17:06.014
I know you want to
help Una. Chris.

341
00:17:06.039 --> 00:17:07.886
but if you take that
stand. this whole case

342
00:17:07.911 --> 00:17:09.216
becomes about you.

343
00:17:09.241 --> 00:17:10.420
You are the captain
of this ship.

344
00:17:10.444 --> 00:17:13.086
You knew Una was an Illyrian.
and you didn't tell Starfleet.

345
00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:14.667
You could be charged
with conspiracy.

346
00:17:14.692 --> 00:17:17.216
and your whole crew
could be at risk.

347
00:17:17.241 --> 00:17:20.113
No inspiring speeches today.

348
00:17:20.138 --> 00:17:22.140
Today. if you want to help Una.

349
00:17:22.165 --> 00:17:24.602
the best thing you can do is
leave the talking to others.

350
00:17:26.558 --> 00:17:27.864
"Mr. Spock.

351
00:17:27.906 --> 00:17:30.562
"I do hope you
understand why I have to

352
00:17:30.605 --> 00:17:32.303
"throw your friend in jail

353
00:17:32.328 --> 00:17:34.584
simply for being who she is."

354
00:17:34.609 --> 00:17:37.134
"Of course. Mr. Pasalk.

355
00:17:37.177 --> 00:17:39.745
"It is only logical.

356
00:17:39.789 --> 00:17:42.879
Shall we play a round of
Kal-toh this weekend?"

357
00:17:42.922 --> 00:17:46.404
"Yes. That would be enjoyable."

358
00:17:48.895 --> 00:17:50.367
You don't see the tension there?

359
00:17:51.278 --> 00:17:52.932
What tension?

360
00:17:52.976 --> 00:17:55.195
They're all. like. buddy-buddy.

361
00:17:55.239 --> 00:17:57.807
Vulcan bros.

362
00:17:57.850 --> 00:17:59.547
Vulcans
may not give much.

363
00:17:59.591 --> 00:18:01.332
but you can read
their body language.

364
00:18:01.801 --> 00:18:03.679
And those two...

365
00:18:05.075 --> 00:18:06.467
hate each other.

366
00:18:11.168 --> 00:18:13.474
Are you messing
with me right now?

367
00:18:23.702 --> 00:18:27.184
I regret that you had to
witness that outburst.

368
00:18:29.329 --> 00:18:30.635
We won't say a word.

369
00:18:30.753 --> 00:18:32.189
- Mm-mmm.
- Thank you. Doctor.

370
00:18:32.232 --> 00:18:34.669
Of all of my father's
former colleagues.

371
00:18:34.694 --> 00:18:38.263
Pasalk truly brings
out the worst in me.

372
00:18:45.593 --> 00:18:47.552
Ensign Uhura.

373
00:18:47.613 --> 00:18:50.878
I need any communications
referencing Commander Chin-Riley

374
00:18:50.903 --> 00:18:52.513
for the last six months.

375
00:18:52.557 --> 00:18:54.820
Okay. I'll collate.

376
00:18:54.864 --> 00:18:58.389
Including all personal
logs. ship-wide.

377
00:19:01.392 --> 00:19:04.569
Sir. with respect.

378
00:19:04.612 --> 00:19:08.225
per Regulation 25. Section B.
all personal logs remain sealed

379
00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:10.383
unless by order of
Starfleet Command.

380
00:19:10.444 --> 00:19:12.707
- Sufficient evidence...
- I know the rules. Ensign.

381
00:19:12.732 --> 00:19:14.168
I'm giving you an order.

382
00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:16.588
You're doing this to help Una.

383
00:19:16.613 --> 00:19:18.789
Right? She's your friend.

384
00:19:18.814 --> 00:19:21.120
your mentor. I understand.

385
00:19:21.238 --> 00:19:23.327
But you are mine.

386
00:19:24.585 --> 00:19:26.086
And giving me an
illegal order will just

387
00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:27.915
get you in trouble
if I follow it.

388
00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:31.248
I don't think the commander
would want that for you.

389
00:19:31.291 --> 00:19:32.945
Neither do I.

390
00:19:32.989 --> 00:19:36.035
We need to find out
who turned her in.

391
00:19:36.079 --> 00:19:38.565
It might well be the
only way to save her.

392
00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:40.251
Then. respectfully.

393
00:19:40.276 --> 00:19:42.756
we're going to have to
find out another way.

394
00:19:42.781 --> 00:19:46.437
- Nyota...
- I'm sorry. No.

395
00:20:03.019 --> 00:20:04.716
This court
is now in session.

396
00:20:04.759 --> 00:20:06.979
Joining me as judges
in this tribunal

397
00:20:07.023 --> 00:20:10.330
are Space Command
Representative Zus Tlaggul and

398
00:20:10.374 --> 00:20:12.550
Starfleet Commander Chiv.

399
00:20:12.593 --> 00:20:15.127
Commander Chin-Riley.
do you consent

400
00:20:15.152 --> 00:20:16.462
to Captain Batel

401
00:20:16.487 --> 00:20:18.531
as the prosecuting officer?

402
00:20:18.864 --> 00:20:19.924
I do.

403
00:20:19.949 --> 00:20:22.429
Let the charges be read.

404
00:20:24.419 --> 00:20:26.887
Lieutenant
commander Una Chin-Riley

405
00:20:26.912 --> 00:20:28.762
has been formally
charged with violating

406
00:20:28.787 --> 00:20:32.616
Starfleet regulation 614-617.

407
00:20:32.697 --> 00:20:35.047
prohibiting permanent
DNA modification.

408
00:20:35.072 --> 00:20:37.717
as well as submitting false
information to Starfleet.

409
00:20:37.742 --> 00:20:40.223
and two counts of sedition.

410
00:20:43.069 --> 00:20:44.810
How do you plead. Commander?

411
00:20:46.279 --> 00:20:49.152
Not guilty.

412
00:20:54.766 --> 00:20:58.030
The Federation's stance
on genetic engineering is clear.

413
00:20:58.074 --> 00:21:01.207
The practice is
dangerous and illegal.

414
00:21:01.251 --> 00:21:02.905
The reasons for this are many.

415
00:21:02.948 --> 00:21:05.342
but the outcome of the
Eugenics Wars on Earth

416
00:21:05.367 --> 00:21:07.413
speaks for itself.

417
00:21:07.474 --> 00:21:09.824
Tens of millions dead.

418
00:21:10.953 --> 00:21:12.324
Pushed to its limits.

419
00:21:12.349 --> 00:21:16.023
genetic engineering is
nothing short of playing God.

420
00:21:16.048 --> 00:21:19.965
By interfering with DNA and
removing genetic outliers.

421
00:21:19.990 --> 00:21:23.555
we endanger the very essence
of natural evolution.

422
00:21:35.513 --> 00:21:36.621
Captain Batel is right.

423
00:21:36.645 --> 00:21:38.517
Permanent genetic modification

424
00:21:38.542 --> 00:21:40.501
is illegal under Federation law.

425
00:21:41.472 --> 00:21:43.032
Slavery was once legal.

426
00:21:43.075 --> 00:21:45.611
Apartheid was legal.

427
00:21:45.636 --> 00:21:48.378
Discrimination against people
for how they worshipped.

428
00:21:48.403 --> 00:21:52.016
how they loved. their gender.
color of their skin...

429
00:21:52.041 --> 00:21:54.043
All legal at one
time or another.

430
00:21:54.068 --> 00:21:57.506
A law does not make
something just.

431
00:21:57.568 --> 00:22:01.311
I'm not saying the
Federation means to do harm.

432
00:22:01.336 --> 00:22:04.165
Their experience with
genetic modification...

433
00:22:04.190 --> 00:22:05.843
The Eugenics Wars...

434
00:22:05.868 --> 00:22:07.767
Was horrific.

435
00:22:08.073 --> 00:22:12.512
The pain that Earth
felt. unimaginable.

436
00:22:12.537 --> 00:22:15.279
The Federation built
a utopia in its wake.

437
00:22:15.304 --> 00:22:17.567
and in an effort to
protect that utopia.

438
00:22:17.592 --> 00:22:20.421
they became blinded by
a centuries-old fear.

439
00:22:20.446 --> 00:22:23.743
so much so that they
have. perhaps unknowingly.

440
00:22:23.768 --> 00:22:26.205
become persecutors.

441
00:22:26.249 --> 00:22:28.773
My client is only here
because of who she is

442
00:22:28.816 --> 00:22:29.971
and because she felt she had

443
00:22:29.996 --> 00:22:32.230
no other choice than
to hide that fact.

444
00:22:32.255 --> 00:22:34.039
Just like the
millions before her

445
00:22:34.064 --> 00:22:35.940
who were forced to hide
how they worshipped.

446
00:22:35.965 --> 00:22:38.279
how they loved. what
they truly looked like.

447
00:22:38.304 --> 00:22:40.002
because it made others

448
00:22:40.027 --> 00:22:41.724
uncomfortable.

449
00:22:41.749 --> 00:22:44.099
Because it made others afraid.

450
00:22:44.124 --> 00:22:47.518
If a law is not just. then I ask

451
00:22:47.618 --> 00:22:51.056
how are we to trust those
who created that law

452
00:22:51.100 --> 00:22:53.264
to serve justice?

453
00:22:53.289 --> 00:22:56.901
The prosecution calls
Admiral Robert April to the stand.

454
00:22:56.966 --> 00:22:59.316
Admiral April. Una Chin-Riley
served under your command

455
00:22:59.341 --> 00:23:01.681
when you were captain of
the USS Enterprise. correct?

456
00:23:01.706 --> 00:23:02.644
Yes.

457
00:23:02.669 --> 00:23:04.469
But before that. you
sponsored her application

458
00:23:04.494 --> 00:23:06.433
- to Starfleet Academy.
- I did.

459
00:23:06.458 --> 00:23:07.437
So would it be fair to say

460
00:23:07.462 --> 00:23:10.570
you have an investment
in Una's career?

461
00:23:12.221 --> 00:23:13.774
It would.

462
00:23:13.940 --> 00:23:15.681
Admiral. I have to ask.

463
00:23:15.706 --> 00:23:18.414
at any point. did Lieutenant
Commander Chin-Riley

464
00:23:18.439 --> 00:23:21.192
disclose to you that she
was genetically modified?

465
00:23:21.217 --> 00:23:23.195
- No.
- If you had known she was genetically modified.

466
00:23:23.219 --> 00:23:25.086
would you have sponsored
her application

467
00:23:25.111 --> 00:23:26.550
to Starfleet Academy?

468
00:23:26.575 --> 00:23:29.094
Una is an extremely
talented officer.

469
00:23:29.138 --> 00:23:31.997
and one of the most gifted
applicants I'd ever met.

470
00:23:32.022 --> 00:23:33.471
That is not the question. sir.

471
00:23:37.069 --> 00:23:39.092
If you had known Una Chin-Riley
was genetically modified.

472
00:23:39.116 --> 00:23:40.866
would you have sponsored
her application

473
00:23:40.891 --> 00:23:42.762
to Starfleet Academy?

474
00:23:43.153 --> 00:23:45.000
You're under oath. sir.

475
00:23:46.666 --> 00:23:48.643
No. I would not.

476
00:23:52.455 --> 00:23:54.109
Thank you. Admiral.

477
00:23:54.206 --> 00:23:58.471
It takes a big man to
admit his mistakes.

478
00:23:58.515 --> 00:24:00.320
I admire that. Admiral.

479
00:24:00.345 --> 00:24:03.435
Just for the record. could
you tell the court why

480
00:24:03.460 --> 00:24:05.723
you would not have sponsored
Commander Chin-Riley's

481
00:24:05.748 --> 00:24:08.108
Starfleet application.
specifically?

482
00:24:08.133 --> 00:24:11.180
Starfleet Regulation
17. Article 12

483
00:24:11.223 --> 00:24:14.298
explicitly prohibits
genetically modified people.

484
00:24:14.323 --> 00:24:17.030
- such as Illyrians. from serving.
- Of course.

485
00:24:17.055 --> 00:24:20.841
You are an honorable.
decorated admiral.

486
00:24:20.885 --> 00:24:23.279
You wouldn't want
to break protocol

487
00:24:23.322 --> 00:24:25.150
for any one
individual applicant.

488
00:24:25.194 --> 00:24:28.289
- Let me stress this is not personal.
- Right.

489
00:24:28.314 --> 00:24:29.702
It's the law.

490
00:24:29.962 --> 00:24:31.113
Admiral April.

491
00:24:31.156 --> 00:24:35.117
can you tell me what
General Order One is?

492
00:24:35.160 --> 00:24:36.922
Objection. Relevance?

493
00:24:36.947 --> 00:24:40.298
I'm curious myself. Tread
carefully. Counselor.

494
00:24:40.337 --> 00:24:42.513
I will. Your Honor. Admiral.

495
00:24:42.695 --> 00:24:45.133
what is General Order One?

496
00:24:45.158 --> 00:24:48.292
No starship may interfere
with the normal development of

497
00:24:48.317 --> 00:24:51.364
- any alien life or society.
- Yes.

498
00:24:51.437 --> 00:24:53.004
A very important law.

499
00:24:53.029 --> 00:24:55.248
So much so that you
now refer to it as

500
00:24:55.273 --> 00:24:56.752
the Prime Directive.

501
00:24:56.777 --> 00:24:59.258
- do you not?
- Yes. that is correct.

502
00:24:59.283 --> 00:25:01.851
In 2246. while in
command of the Enterprise.

503
00:25:01.876 --> 00:25:04.967
you chose to warn the Perricans.
a pre-warp civilization.

504
00:25:04.992 --> 00:25:07.316
about a possibly
apocalyptic meteor shower

505
00:25:07.341 --> 00:25:08.864
about to hit their planet.

506
00:25:08.889 --> 00:25:11.979
Were you then following
General Order One?

507
00:25:12.023 --> 00:25:14.373
- That was different.
- 2248.

508
00:25:14.398 --> 00:25:17.488
You sent your science officer
to the industrial-age planet

509
00:25:17.513 --> 00:25:19.559
Na'rel to solve
the imminent threat

510
00:25:19.584 --> 00:25:21.151
of an extinction-level drought

511
00:25:21.176 --> 00:25:23.618
by sharing Federation
technology.

512
00:25:23.643 --> 00:25:26.848
- Were you in compliance then?
- Objection. Relevance again.

513
00:25:26.873 --> 00:25:28.461
An entire planet
would have died.

514
00:25:28.486 --> 00:25:31.309
And when you landed on the
hostile planet Man-us 2

515
00:25:31.334 --> 00:25:33.447
without your security officer.

516
00:25:33.472 --> 00:25:35.648
you chose to reveal
your starship

517
00:25:35.673 --> 00:25:37.893
to the pre-warp
civilization Ohawk.

518
00:25:37.918 --> 00:25:40.269
- Objection!
- Did you comply then. Admiral?

519
00:25:40.312 --> 00:25:42.009
Counselor.
I will remind you

520
00:25:42.053 --> 00:25:44.229
the witness is
not on trial here.

521
00:25:44.273 --> 00:25:47.728
Admiral. it would seem
that the rules of Starfleet

522
00:25:47.753 --> 00:25:50.645
only apply when a captain
deems that they do.

523
00:25:53.820 --> 00:25:55.822
Is there a question. Counselor?

524
00:25:55.847 --> 00:25:57.400
Yes.

525
00:25:58.321 --> 00:26:00.453
You have shown
that you have been

526
00:26:00.478 --> 00:26:02.523
repeatedly willing to break

527
00:26:02.548 --> 00:26:05.072
the very first
order of Starfleet

528
00:26:05.100 --> 00:26:07.227
and you are hailed as a hero.

529
00:26:07.252 --> 00:26:11.213
You can break the law if
you so choose. So. hiding

530
00:26:11.256 --> 00:26:13.398
behind order and protocol
to explain why you would

531
00:26:13.423 --> 00:26:15.730
not have admitted Una
Chin-Riley to Starfleet

532
00:26:15.755 --> 00:26:17.498
is a sanctimonious
falsehood. is it not?

533
00:26:17.523 --> 00:26:20.047
- Objection!
- Counselor!

534
00:26:20.072 --> 00:26:22.916
You will cease this line
of questioning at once.

535
00:26:22.941 --> 00:26:25.985
My client did not ask to
be genetically modified.

536
00:26:26.010 --> 00:26:28.201
It is an Illyrian
cultural practice

537
00:26:28.226 --> 00:26:30.600
done to children before
they are even born.

538
00:26:30.625 --> 00:26:31.887
It is done for survival.

539
00:26:31.912 --> 00:26:34.001
and yet she has been arrested

540
00:26:34.026 --> 00:26:35.964
because of a violation of a law.

541
00:26:35.989 --> 00:26:39.123
But the admiral has just shown
us that Starfleet regulations

542
00:26:39.148 --> 00:26:41.827
are flimsy and
subjective at best.

543
00:26:41.852 --> 00:26:45.464
Starfleet captains make
judgement calls every day.

544
00:26:45.508 --> 00:26:47.074
Calls that save lives.

545
00:26:47.099 --> 00:26:49.057
Una Chin-Riley's
services to Starfleet

546
00:26:49.082 --> 00:26:50.649
have been commendable. yes.

547
00:26:50.674 --> 00:26:53.160
But the law that she broke
is there to save lives

548
00:26:53.185 --> 00:26:55.144
and prevent genocide.

549
00:26:55.169 --> 00:26:57.433
So. if you ask me. Counselor.

550
00:26:57.458 --> 00:26:59.330
if I would have denied
Commander Chin-Riley's

551
00:26:59.355 --> 00:27:01.275
access to Starfleet
Academy had I known

552
00:27:01.300 --> 00:27:02.693
she was genetically modified.

553
00:27:02.718 --> 00:27:05.721
my answer is still
yes. I would have.

554
00:27:08.248 --> 00:27:10.174
So you admit that the
reason for your decision

555
00:27:10.215 --> 00:27:12.379
is not law. but fear
and racial prejudice.

556
00:27:12.404 --> 00:27:15.755
- Objection!
- Sustained. - Counselor Ketoul.

557
00:27:15.780 --> 00:27:18.086
this is a court martial
for Una Chin-Riley.

558
00:27:18.111 --> 00:27:19.703
not Admiral April.

559
00:27:19.728 --> 00:27:21.965
That you are unable
to defend your client

560
00:27:21.990 --> 00:27:23.871
does not permit you to
attack the Federation

561
00:27:23.896 --> 00:27:26.070
or our officers.

562
00:27:26.095 --> 00:27:28.825
All of the admiral's
testimony will be stricken

563
00:27:28.850 --> 00:27:30.634
from the court record.

564
00:27:33.478 --> 00:27:35.828
Did Una's lawyer just try
and indict Admiral April?

565
00:27:35.853 --> 00:27:37.202
It would appear so.

566
00:27:37.227 --> 00:27:38.628
I guess that's one strategy.

567
00:27:38.653 --> 00:27:41.016
That didn't exactly
make April look good.

568
00:27:41.041 --> 00:27:43.914
But how does any
of this help Una?

569
00:27:45.444 --> 00:27:47.446
Oh. boy.

570
00:27:47.476 --> 00:27:49.913
So. the lawyer was your idea.

571
00:27:50.050 --> 00:27:51.313
She was.

572
00:27:52.749 --> 00:27:54.293
She's one of the best
civil rights litigators

573
00:27:54.317 --> 00:27:56.710
in the galaxy. and Una's friend.

574
00:27:59.153 --> 00:28:00.764
You know. I think highly of Una.

575
00:28:00.887 --> 00:28:04.468
Promoted her faster than any
other officer on my ship.

576
00:28:04.493 --> 00:28:06.844
Recommended her for
the Medal of Gallantry

577
00:28:06.869 --> 00:28:09.915
after the Marcel
disaster in 2248.

578
00:28:09.940 --> 00:28:11.898
Yeah. I know.

579
00:28:11.942 --> 00:28:13.952
It's a shame the rest of the
court didn't get a chance

580
00:28:13.976 --> 00:28:15.674
to hear that today.

581
00:28:29.996 --> 00:28:31.962
What the hell was that?

582
00:28:32.005 --> 00:28:33.267
You're supposed to defend me.

583
00:28:33.311 --> 00:28:34.617
not attack Admiral April.

584
00:28:34.660 --> 00:28:37.620
- not indict the Federation.
- Why not?

585
00:28:37.663 --> 00:28:39.926
Why are you still
trying to protect them?

586
00:28:39.951 --> 00:28:42.170
I thought you said you
were ready for this fight.

587
00:28:42.195 --> 00:28:45.345
Do you know how rare it is
to get a platform like this?

588
00:28:45.591 --> 00:28:46.564
Platform?

589
00:28:46.589 --> 00:28:49.548
Most Illyrians don't
have your privilege.

590
00:28:49.573 --> 00:28:51.378
Has it occurred to you that
your case might bring us

591
00:28:51.402 --> 00:28:53.752
one step closer in
dismantling the law?

592
00:28:53.777 --> 00:28:57.477
Maybe in the future there
can be justice for Illyrians.

593
00:28:57.502 --> 00:28:59.069
I thought you knew that.

594
00:28:59.094 --> 00:29:01.923
All you ever wanted
here was a soapbox.

595
00:29:01.948 --> 00:29:03.515
This isn't about defending me.

596
00:29:03.540 --> 00:29:05.363
This is just a way for you
to broadcast your hatred

597
00:29:05.387 --> 00:29:07.040
of the Federation.

598
00:29:07.065 --> 00:29:10.460
I thought you were here to
help me. but you're not.

599
00:29:10.485 --> 00:29:12.365
As long as you can make
the Federation look bad.

600
00:29:12.390 --> 00:29:14.456
then who the hell cares if I
get left behind in the process?

601
00:29:14.480 --> 00:29:19.128
I think we both know you're not
the one who gets left behind.

602
00:29:20.609 --> 00:29:22.350
Neera...

603
00:29:22.375 --> 00:29:24.290
That's all in the past.

604
00:29:24.406 --> 00:29:25.842
We should talk about it.

605
00:29:25.885 --> 00:29:27.365
Please.

606
00:29:27.409 --> 00:29:29.802
I told you that I would try.

607
00:29:30.082 --> 00:29:32.544
And that's exactly
what I'm doing.

608
00:29:32.787 --> 00:29:34.452
Because at least with me.

609
00:29:34.477 --> 00:29:36.522
what you see is what you get.

610
00:29:39.072 --> 00:29:41.814
Now. if you'll excuse
me. I have work to do.

611
00:29:53.146 --> 00:29:54.875
The defense calls to the stand

612
00:29:54.900 --> 00:29:57.598
three expert
character witnesses.

613
00:29:57.942 --> 00:29:59.335
La'An Noonien-Singh.

614
00:29:59.360 --> 00:30:01.606
security officer for
the USS Enterprise.

615
00:30:01.631 --> 00:30:03.589
I am the chief science officer.

616
00:30:03.614 --> 00:30:07.270
Chief medical officer
of the USS Enterprise.

617
00:30:07.295 --> 00:30:10.168
I graduated top of my class
and have been promoted

618
00:30:10.193 --> 00:30:12.064
each year during my
tenure in Starfleet.

619
00:30:12.089 --> 00:30:13.623
You were also in consideration

620
00:30:13.648 --> 00:30:15.848
- for the Starfleet Medal of Gallantry.
- Yes.

621
00:30:15.873 --> 00:30:18.170
- So you've saved lives?
- Yes.

622
00:30:18.195 --> 00:30:20.828
When did you first
meet Una Chin-Riley?

623
00:30:20.853 --> 00:30:23.900
On my first day as an
ensign on the Enterprise.

624
00:30:23.925 --> 00:30:25.771
She was part of
the rescue mission

625
00:30:25.796 --> 00:30:29.147
that found me after I escaped
from a Gorn breeding planet.

626
00:30:29.172 --> 00:30:30.882
You have a very
unique last name.

627
00:30:30.907 --> 00:30:34.476
- Do you have any relation to Khan Noonien Singh?
- Yes.

628
00:30:34.501 --> 00:30:37.043
Did you ever suspect
Una to be an Illyrian?

629
00:30:37.087 --> 00:30:39.132
No. I did not.

630
00:30:43.176 --> 00:30:45.353
Did you ever get the sense
that Commander Chin-Riley

631
00:30:45.378 --> 00:30:47.153
was hiding something?

632
00:30:48.603 --> 00:30:50.256
Never.

633
00:30:54.191 --> 00:30:57.150
Just that she was
discreet and empathetic

634
00:30:57.175 --> 00:31:00.570
and handled personal
matters with great care.

635
00:31:00.595 --> 00:31:04.817
Yes. I did get the sense that
she was hiding something.

636
00:31:04.842 --> 00:31:06.888
What was she hiding?

637
00:31:12.080 --> 00:31:15.753
An affinity for Gilbert
and Sullivan musicals.

638
00:31:19.747 --> 00:31:23.350
After the defendant rescued
you. did you remain close?

639
00:31:24.374 --> 00:31:26.681
I had no family left.

640
00:31:26.706 --> 00:31:28.882
Una made sure I
was taken care of.

641
00:31:29.056 --> 00:31:32.202
She sponsored my
application to Starfleet.

642
00:31:32.227 --> 00:31:34.272
Would it be fair to say that

643
00:31:34.297 --> 00:31:36.513
you would not have
joined Starfleet

644
00:31:36.538 --> 00:31:39.802
if not for Commander Chin-Riley?

645
00:31:39.845 --> 00:31:43.370
Counselor. I wouldn't be
alive if it weren't for Una.

646
00:31:43.414 --> 00:31:45.634
And the people you
saved during your career.

647
00:31:45.677 --> 00:31:47.549
would they be alive?

648
00:31:48.593 --> 00:31:51.378
No. they would not.

649
00:31:53.013 --> 00:31:55.443
Mr. Spock. if the
defendant broke the law.

650
00:31:55.468 --> 00:31:57.601
would it follow that the
only logical course of action

651
00:31:57.626 --> 00:31:59.672
is for her to be
punished accordingly?

652
00:31:59.697 --> 00:32:02.753
Perhaps. Although I
think it is illogical

653
00:32:02.778 --> 00:32:04.388
for Starfleet to punish itself.

654
00:32:04.413 --> 00:32:06.154
I'm afraid I don't understand.

655
00:32:07.537 --> 00:32:09.183
The loss of Una
would be destructive

656
00:32:09.208 --> 00:32:10.753
to Starfleet as an organization.

657
00:32:12.486 --> 00:32:14.837
She is an extraordinary officer.

658
00:32:17.876 --> 00:32:19.790
Please describe the nature
of your relationship

659
00:32:19.815 --> 00:32:21.164
with the defendant.

660
00:32:21.207 --> 00:32:22.600
She is a mentor.

661
00:32:22.625 --> 00:32:24.378
I have learned a great
deal about leadership

662
00:32:24.403 --> 00:32:25.950
by serving under her.

663
00:32:25.975 --> 00:32:30.197
She puts the lives of her
crew above her own. Always.

664
00:32:30.222 --> 00:32:31.789
She is a friend.

665
00:32:31.813 --> 00:32:34.594
Family. Una is

666
00:32:34.619 --> 00:32:36.186
family.

667
00:32:47.913 --> 00:32:49.939
Thank you. Lieutenant.

668
00:32:50.015 --> 00:32:53.198
Volume 12.9 of the
Starfleet Uniform

669
00:32:53.223 --> 00:32:54.877
Code of Justice.

670
00:32:54.920 --> 00:32:56.930
If you need anything
else. I will...

671
00:32:56.955 --> 00:32:58.857
Lieutenant. there is one
more thing. I was wondering.

672
00:32:58.881 --> 00:33:00.433
did you have any
luck finding out

673
00:33:00.458 --> 00:33:03.635
how the prosecution learned
that Una was Illyrian?

674
00:33:03.817 --> 00:33:06.341
No. not-not so far.

675
00:33:06.366 --> 00:33:09.500
But you have an idea
about it. don't you?

676
00:33:11.284 --> 00:33:13.286
You think it was you.

677
00:33:14.984 --> 00:33:16.725
Yes.

678
00:33:16.768 --> 00:33:18.297
Why is that?

679
00:33:18.322 --> 00:33:19.668
The night I found out

680
00:33:19.693 --> 00:33:22.685
Una was Illyrian. I was...

681
00:33:24.471 --> 00:33:26.082
I was angry.

682
00:33:26.125 --> 00:33:28.040
I recorded a personal log.

683
00:33:28.084 --> 00:33:30.300
And you think that
somebody got ahold

684
00:33:30.325 --> 00:33:31.935
of that personal log.

685
00:33:31.960 --> 00:33:34.223
and that's how Una was exposed.

686
00:33:34.287 --> 00:33:36.028
- Yes.
- Interesting.

687
00:33:36.053 --> 00:33:38.229
May I ask why you were angry?

688
00:33:38.298 --> 00:33:42.172
It can't be because Una
was genetically augmented.

689
00:33:42.201 --> 00:33:44.682
Considering your last
name. I would think

690
00:33:44.707 --> 00:33:46.273
you would understand the nuances

691
00:33:46.298 --> 00:33:48.203
of genetic manipulation
better than most.

692
00:33:49.141 --> 00:33:51.164
Una was my friend.
She lied to me.

693
00:33:51.189 --> 00:33:53.278
It's not that simple. is it?

694
00:33:54.186 --> 00:33:56.348
- No.
- Could it be

695
00:33:56.373 --> 00:33:59.936
that you carry your
family's augmentations.

696
00:33:59.961 --> 00:34:02.833
and you believe
that because of them

697
00:34:02.858 --> 00:34:04.947
you may become dangerous?

698
00:34:06.339 --> 00:34:08.298
Yes. I do.

699
00:34:11.301 --> 00:34:14.086
There is nothing wrong
with you. Lieutenant.

700
00:34:16.101 --> 00:34:18.887
No hidden monster inside.

701
00:34:18.912 --> 00:34:20.232
- You don't know that.
- But I do.

702
00:34:20.257 --> 00:34:21.640
It's how they make us feel.

703
00:34:22.920 --> 00:34:24.824
They look down at
us for so long that

704
00:34:24.849 --> 00:34:27.128
we begin to look
down at ourselves.

705
00:34:28.753 --> 00:34:30.275
Genetics is not destiny.

706
00:34:30.300 --> 00:34:33.215
despite what you may
have been taught.

707
00:34:33.279 --> 00:34:36.108
The fear you have of
yourself. it's not your own.

708
00:34:36.152 --> 00:34:38.154
It was drilled into you.

709
00:34:38.197 --> 00:34:41.061
You're not born a monster.

710
00:34:41.086 --> 00:34:44.193
You were just born with
a capacity for actions.

711
00:34:44.218 --> 00:34:46.552
good or ill.

712
00:34:46.597 --> 00:34:48.338
Just like the rest of us.

713
00:34:50.862 --> 00:34:52.994
In any case...

714
00:34:54.039 --> 00:34:56.999
it takes six months at a minimum

715
00:34:57.042 --> 00:34:58.435
after a request

716
00:34:58.478 --> 00:35:00.916
from a boatload of admirals

717
00:35:00.941 --> 00:35:03.465
to subpoena a personal log.

718
00:35:03.527 --> 00:35:06.138
They haven't had
nearly that long.

719
00:35:06.182 --> 00:35:07.991
I guarantee. you
are not the person

720
00:35:08.016 --> 00:35:10.714
who leaked Una's true
identity to Starfleet.

721
00:35:17.400 --> 00:35:20.040
But if it wasn't my log
that caused this. then

722
00:35:20.065 --> 00:35:22.154
who turned in Una?

723
00:35:22.179 --> 00:35:24.529
You're head of security here.

724
00:35:24.554 --> 00:35:26.948
Una speaks highly of you.

725
00:35:26.973 --> 00:35:30.063
which is not something
she does of many people.

726
00:35:30.088 --> 00:35:32.525
Who do you think did it?

727
00:35:32.996 --> 00:35:35.346
I-I d... I don't know.

728
00:35:36.774 --> 00:35:39.255
Someone who could gain
from exposing the truth.

729
00:35:39.345 --> 00:35:41.391
My thoughts exactly.

730
00:35:43.045 --> 00:35:46.700
Thank you. You've
been very helpful.

731
00:35:48.120 --> 00:35:50.732
Why do I feel like I've
just been hit by a shuttle?

732
00:35:50.757 --> 00:35:52.803
I'll take that as a compliment.

733
00:36:02.971 --> 00:36:04.606
I would like to
call the defendant

734
00:36:04.631 --> 00:36:06.808
Una Chin-Riley to the stand.

735
00:36:14.598 --> 00:36:16.774
How long have you
been in Starfleet?

736
00:36:16.818 --> 00:36:18.976
Twenty-five years.

737
00:36:19.001 --> 00:36:22.396
Would you call this
career your life's goal?

738
00:36:22.421 --> 00:36:24.108
It's all I've ever wanted.

739
00:36:24.133 --> 00:36:27.827
You knew you were Illyrian.
thus genetically modified.

740
00:36:27.852 --> 00:36:29.767
Didn't you think you
might find yourself

741
00:36:29.792 --> 00:36:31.837
in this position one day?

742
00:36:31.862 --> 00:36:33.843
I had been warned. yes.

743
00:36:33.868 --> 00:36:35.802
So why join Starfleet?

744
00:36:37.664 --> 00:36:40.755
Ad astra per aspera.

745
00:36:40.780 --> 00:36:42.934
Could you translate
for the court?

746
00:36:45.542 --> 00:36:48.893
"To the stars through hardship."

747
00:36:48.937 --> 00:36:52.244
It was the Starfleet motto
before the Federation.

748
00:36:52.288 --> 00:36:54.333
I learned it studying
history in school.

749
00:36:54.358 --> 00:36:57.187
Why were you drawn
to that motto?

750
00:36:57.249 --> 00:37:00.252
I knew it meant we
must endure hardship

751
00:37:00.296 --> 00:37:01.906
to get to the stars.

752
00:37:01.931 --> 00:37:03.889
But I like to think
that it also means

753
00:37:03.914 --> 00:37:06.003
that the stars could deliver us

754
00:37:06.028 --> 00:37:08.496
from anything. That

755
00:37:08.521 --> 00:37:11.568
in the mystery an
vastness of space.

756
00:37:11.611 --> 00:37:14.223
we might not just
satisfy our curiosity.

757
00:37:14.729 --> 00:37:16.790
our need for exploration.

758
00:37:16.834 --> 00:37:21.143
but that in it. we
might each also find...

759
00:37:21.168 --> 00:37:23.214
salvation.

760
00:37:24.320 --> 00:37:26.278
Why would you need salvation?

761
00:37:28.104 --> 00:37:30.193
Was your childhood difficult?

762
00:37:31.571 --> 00:37:33.976
Objection. The defendant's
childhood isn't relevant here.

763
00:37:34.001 --> 00:37:36.873
I'm simply
establishing context.

764
00:37:36.898 --> 00:37:40.118
If Una Chin-Riley is to be
tried for being an Illyrian.

765
00:37:40.162 --> 00:37:44.035
then the court must understand
what it means to be an Illyrian.

766
00:37:44.079 --> 00:37:46.820
We'll allow it to
continue. Counselor.

767
00:37:46.864 --> 00:37:48.170
Thank you.

768
00:37:48.213 --> 00:37:50.302
You grew up in a
Federation colony

769
00:37:50.346 --> 00:37:52.696
in the Vaultera Nebula. correct?

770
00:37:52.739 --> 00:37:55.220
Yes. We were given
provisional membership

771
00:37:55.264 --> 00:37:57.534
in the Federation the
year before I was born.

772
00:37:57.559 --> 00:38:00.191
On the condition that
all genetic modification

773
00:38:00.216 --> 00:38:02.333
was to cease. Is that correct?

774
00:38:02.358 --> 00:38:05.535
- Yes.
- But that didn't happen. did it?

775
00:38:07.711 --> 00:38:10.366
It did for some.

776
00:38:10.409 --> 00:38:13.760
But for other
families. like mine.

777
00:38:13.804 --> 00:38:16.763
it was our tradition.

778
00:38:16.807 --> 00:38:18.746
Our heritage.

779
00:38:18.771 --> 00:38:21.551
What was life like
for your family

780
00:38:21.594 --> 00:38:23.596
under the Federation?

781
00:38:25.628 --> 00:38:27.818
We no longer
discussed our customs.

782
00:38:27.861 --> 00:38:30.995
We performed our
rituals only in secret.

783
00:38:31.039 --> 00:38:34.087
Those who could hid
their modifications.

784
00:38:34.112 --> 00:38:37.001
When new children
were born. parents

785
00:38:37.026 --> 00:38:39.995
sought out friendly
doctors to deliver them.

786
00:38:41.130 --> 00:38:42.827
We knew if we were
ever found to be

787
00:38:42.852 --> 00:38:45.158
genetically augmented
we would be arrested.

788
00:38:45.221 --> 00:38:47.919
Did that ever happen
to anyone you knew?

789
00:38:48.083 --> 00:38:50.710
A boy I went to school with.

790
00:38:50.735 --> 00:38:52.563
Ivan Ketoul.

791
00:38:52.716 --> 00:38:55.197
He was my best friend's cousin.

792
00:38:55.222 --> 00:38:57.224
What happened to him?

793
00:38:57.249 --> 00:38:59.694
Some of us have immune
systems that can glow.

794
00:38:59.719 --> 00:39:04.115
Someone must have seen
him. He came home one day

795
00:39:04.159 --> 00:39:07.031
to find the word "augment"
on their door. We had just

796
00:39:07.075 --> 00:39:09.033
learned about
augments in school.

797
00:39:09.077 --> 00:39:11.993
Opinions on them were clear.

798
00:39:13.450 --> 00:39:15.626
Someone must have found out.

799
00:39:16.171 --> 00:39:17.955
Maybe it was just a prank.

800
00:39:17.999 --> 00:39:19.957
Did anyone defend him.

801
00:39:20.001 --> 00:39:21.306
his family?

802
00:39:22.159 --> 00:39:23.987
Some.

803
00:39:24.012 --> 00:39:26.206
But there weren't enough voices.

804
00:39:27.680 --> 00:39:30.421
Ivan and his parents were
arrested in their home.

805
00:39:30.446 --> 00:39:32.013
He was ten years old.

806
00:39:34.868 --> 00:39:36.958
How did this affect
your community?

807
00:39:36.983 --> 00:39:38.985
Some families moved
to other planets

808
00:39:39.010 --> 00:39:40.968
that weren't Federation.

809
00:39:40.995 --> 00:39:43.214
And those of us who stayed.

810
00:39:43.372 --> 00:39:46.114
we were persecuted.

811
00:39:48.009 --> 00:39:50.409
Circumstances became extreme.

812
00:39:52.230 --> 00:39:54.923
The anti-augmentation
laws seemed to give people

813
00:39:54.948 --> 00:39:58.300
freedom to act on
their worst impulses.

814
00:39:59.736 --> 00:40:01.781
First were the insults.

815
00:40:02.682 --> 00:40:03.758
"Augment."

816
00:40:03.783 --> 00:40:05.872
"Moddie."

817
00:40:05.897 --> 00:40:07.855
"Freak."

818
00:40:07.918 --> 00:40:10.013
There were stores that
wouldn't serve you

819
00:40:10.038 --> 00:40:11.976
if they'd heard
you'd been modified.

820
00:40:14.100 --> 00:40:15.833
Even the rumors
could be dangerous.

821
00:40:15.858 --> 00:40:18.904
I remember when
the attacks began.

822
00:40:18.929 --> 00:40:21.149
We feared for our lives.

823
00:40:22.619 --> 00:40:24.055
Go on.

824
00:40:24.178 --> 00:40:26.514
There was a fight
at school one day.

825
00:40:27.640 --> 00:40:30.478
One boy accused another
boy of being an Illyrian.

826
00:40:31.985 --> 00:40:33.422
I tried to stop it.

827
00:40:33.465 --> 00:40:35.598
My leg got broken.

828
00:40:35.623 --> 00:40:37.625
It was such a simple fix.

829
00:40:38.905 --> 00:40:41.236
So easy to treat
with modern medicine.

830
00:40:42.045 --> 00:40:44.091
But my parents wouldn't
take me to a hospital.

831
00:40:44.141 --> 00:40:46.306
They were afraid.

832
00:40:46.331 --> 00:40:50.683
Despite my modifications.
my leg became infected.

833
00:40:52.080 --> 00:40:53.690
If we hadn't found
and Illyrian doctor

834
00:40:53.715 --> 00:40:55.558
willing to see me in
the middle of the night.

835
00:40:55.583 --> 00:40:56.863
I would have died.

836
00:41:02.715 --> 00:41:05.383
I'm so sorry.

837
00:41:05.584 --> 00:41:08.152
Was this normal for

838
00:41:08.177 --> 00:41:11.326
such a common thing to
become life-threatening?

839
00:41:11.351 --> 00:41:13.524
It was for kids like me. yes.

840
00:41:13.549 --> 00:41:15.718
Civil unrest became so great

841
00:41:15.743 --> 00:41:19.138
the local government decided
to divide us into two cities:

842
00:41:19.163 --> 00:41:21.600
Illyrian and non-Illyrian.

843
00:41:22.906 --> 00:41:24.299
Thank you.

844
00:41:26.049 --> 00:41:29.376
My family. we went to
the non-Illyrian city.

845
00:41:31.011 --> 00:41:33.353
You see. some of us could pass.

846
00:41:35.380 --> 00:41:37.339
We could blend in.

847
00:41:37.364 --> 00:41:39.149
so we did.

848
00:41:40.318 --> 00:41:43.930
We left everyone else
behind. Our families.

849
00:41:45.929 --> 00:41:47.974
Our friends.

850
00:41:48.018 --> 00:41:50.063
We left them all.

851
00:41:51.017 --> 00:41:53.019
I regret it to this day.

852
00:41:54.704 --> 00:41:56.662
I'm so sorry.

853
00:41:57.622 --> 00:41:58.884
And yet.

854
00:41:59.048 --> 00:42:02.153
after all of this strife.

855
00:42:02.178 --> 00:42:05.007
you still wanted to be
a Starfleet officer.

856
00:42:05.032 --> 00:42:06.854
Yes.

857
00:42:07.255 --> 00:42:10.020
One last question. Commander.

858
00:42:11.219 --> 00:42:14.056
How did Starfleet find out
that you were Illyrian?

859
00:42:15.025 --> 00:42:18.110
You managed to keep your status
a secret for so many years.

860
00:42:18.135 --> 00:42:20.006
it's surprising
they found out now.

861
00:42:20.050 --> 00:42:23.369
- I don't...
- Who turned you in to Starfleet?

862
00:42:23.394 --> 00:42:25.091
I remind you. you
are under oath.

863
00:42:25.116 --> 00:42:27.640
I caution you against
badgering your own witness.

864
00:42:27.665 --> 00:42:29.780
- Who turned you in?
- Counselor!

865
00:42:29.805 --> 00:42:30.849
I did.

866
00:42:33.796 --> 00:42:35.722
I turned myself in.

867
00:42:41.670 --> 00:42:42.758
Why?

868
00:42:43.822 --> 00:42:46.042
Why would you risk your career.

869
00:42:46.067 --> 00:42:48.635
the life you built?

870
00:42:48.731 --> 00:42:52.169
I was so sick of living a lie.

871
00:42:52.213 --> 00:42:54.954
of pretending to be
someone I wasn't.

872
00:42:56.129 --> 00:42:58.016
I wanted my crew...

873
00:42:58.915 --> 00:43:02.440
I wanted my crew to know
me for who I really was.

874
00:43:02.465 --> 00:43:06.251
I thought maybe if they did.
I would finally be safe.

875
00:43:08.660 --> 00:43:12.538
And Starfleet would finally
understand Illyrian's better.

876
00:43:12.563 --> 00:43:14.914
So. after all of it...

877
00:43:16.668 --> 00:43:19.432
you still wanted
Starfleet to accept you.

878
00:43:19.457 --> 00:43:20.893
Why?

879
00:43:20.918 --> 00:43:22.702
When I was five or six.

880
00:43:22.727 --> 00:43:25.594
I remember a Starfleet
crew visited.

881
00:43:27.422 --> 00:43:30.180
They were all so...

882
00:43:30.324 --> 00:43:32.717
different from one another.

883
00:43:32.742 --> 00:43:35.745
So many crew members
from so many planets.

884
00:43:35.770 --> 00:43:39.296
It was beautiful. I thought

885
00:43:39.321 --> 00:43:43.064
if all those people
from all those worlds

886
00:43:43.115 --> 00:43:46.597
can work together. side by side.

887
00:43:47.062 --> 00:43:49.226
maybe I could. too.

888
00:43:49.270 --> 00:43:53.274
Maybe I could be a part of
something bigger than myself.

889
00:43:53.317 --> 00:43:56.755
Starfleet is not a
perfect organization.

890
00:43:56.799 --> 00:43:58.931
but it strives to be.

891
00:43:58.975 --> 00:44:02.021
And I believe it could be.

892
00:44:03.022 --> 00:44:05.568
You're saying that...

893
00:44:06.374 --> 00:44:09.551
is why you turned yourself in?

894
00:44:09.594 --> 00:44:11.074
Yes.

895
00:44:11.117 --> 00:44:14.599
Because you believe
in Starfleet.

896
00:44:15.529 --> 00:44:16.786
Yes.

897
00:44:18.259 --> 00:44:21.605
Ad astra per aspera.

898
00:44:25.462 --> 00:44:27.551
Thank you. Commander.

899
00:44:28.494 --> 00:44:30.716
No further questions.

900
00:44:42.497 --> 00:44:45.064
That was a very emotional story.

901
00:44:46.407 --> 00:44:49.323
However. emotions
are irrelevant.

902
00:44:49.526 --> 00:44:51.462
Facts are not.

903
00:44:51.487 --> 00:44:54.627
On what date did
Captain Christopher Pike

904
00:44:54.652 --> 00:44:56.480
learn the truth about your

905
00:44:56.505 --> 00:44:58.420
genetically modified status?

906
00:44:58.953 --> 00:45:00.428
Objection.

907
00:45:00.453 --> 00:45:02.777
This trial is about
Una Chin-Riley.

908
00:45:02.802 --> 00:45:04.081
not her captain.

909
00:45:04.106 --> 00:45:06.064
What we have here is
not just one officer's

910
00:45:06.089 --> 00:45:08.047
violation of the law.

911
00:45:08.072 --> 00:45:10.422
This incident is evidence of
breakdown of chain of command

912
00:45:10.447 --> 00:45:12.415
on board the
starship Enterprise.

913
00:45:12.440 --> 00:45:15.145
starting with its captain.

914
00:45:15.170 --> 00:45:18.353
If Captain Pike was aware
of Una Chin-Riley's fraud

915
00:45:18.378 --> 00:45:22.207
prior to her arrest. and
did not notify Starfleet.

916
00:45:22.232 --> 00:45:24.452
then what we have
here is not fraud.

917
00:45:24.477 --> 00:45:26.305
but conspiracy.

918
00:45:27.401 --> 00:45:30.578
Since my co-counsel
neglected to elicit testimony

919
00:45:30.603 --> 00:45:32.213
from the parties involved.

920
00:45:32.238 --> 00:45:34.458
I will ask the
commander directly.

921
00:45:36.133 --> 00:45:40.093
When did Captain Pike
become aware of your status?

922
00:45:47.823 --> 00:45:49.690
I will also remind the commander

923
00:45:49.715 --> 00:45:51.891
that she is under oath.

924
00:45:52.044 --> 00:45:53.998
And I reminder her that

925
00:45:54.023 --> 00:45:56.546
she does not want
to perjure herself

926
00:45:56.571 --> 00:45:58.834
as I ask one more time.

927
00:45:58.877 --> 00:46:01.400
when did Christopher
Pike first learn

928
00:46:01.425 --> 00:46:03.882
that you were an Illyrian?

929
00:46:11.140 --> 00:46:13.490
Stardate 1224.3

930
00:46:17.069 --> 00:46:18.506
Four months.

931
00:46:18.916 --> 00:46:21.857
Well before your arrest.

932
00:46:22.367 --> 00:46:24.076
For four months.

933
00:46:24.120 --> 00:46:25.991
the captain of the Enterprise

934
00:46:26.016 --> 00:46:27.916
engaged in a conspiracy

935
00:46:27.941 --> 00:46:30.918
to conceal the Illyrian
Una Chin-Riley.

936
00:46:32.515 --> 00:46:34.703
I have no further questions.

937
00:46:47.609 --> 00:46:49.894
The defense wants
you to ignore the facts

938
00:46:49.919 --> 00:46:51.529
in favor of emotion.

939
00:46:51.554 --> 00:46:55.343
But the only matter of
import today is the law.

940
00:46:55.368 --> 00:46:57.326
Una Chin-Riley

941
00:46:57.351 --> 00:46:59.440
broke the law and lied about it.

942
00:46:59.465 --> 00:47:02.642
as her own testimony
has proven. Further.

943
00:47:02.667 --> 00:47:05.212
her actions will likely
lead to a court martial of

944
00:47:05.237 --> 00:47:07.848
one of Starfleet's most
decorated officers.

945
00:47:08.120 --> 00:47:10.688
She is clearly
toxic to Starfleet

946
00:47:10.732 --> 00:47:13.645
in both action an inaction.

947
00:47:13.670 --> 00:47:15.716
Therefore. the only
logical response

948
00:47:15.741 --> 00:47:19.745
is to find the defendant
guilty of all charges.

949
00:47:27.488 --> 00:47:30.731
Captain Batel. are
you familiar with

950
00:47:30.756 --> 00:47:33.754
the Starfleet Code 8514?

951
00:47:35.052 --> 00:47:36.575
I am.

952
00:47:37.019 --> 00:47:39.238
Would you mind reading
that code for the court?

953
00:47:43.397 --> 00:47:45.916
"In extraordinary
and extreme circumstances.

954
00:47:45.941 --> 00:47:48.073
"if the following
conditions are met:

955
00:47:48.117 --> 00:47:51.911
any person
fleeing persecution...

956
00:47:51.936 --> 00:47:53.721
We were persecuted.

957
00:47:53.746 --> 00:47:55.771
I remember when
the attacks began.

958
00:47:56.597 --> 00:47:59.190
"or fearing for their
life due to political

959
00:47:59.215 --> 00:48:00.363
"or religious beliefs.

960
00:48:00.388 --> 00:48:01.869
"cultural engagements or

961
00:48:01.894 --> 00:48:04.064
"biological truths may.

962
00:48:04.089 --> 00:48:07.832
seek safety
within Starfleet...

963
00:48:07.857 --> 00:48:10.555
I thought maybe if they did.
I would finally be safe.

964
00:48:10.580 --> 00:48:11.842
We feared for our lives.

965
00:48:13.550 --> 00:48:15.900
"upon revealing
themselves to authorities

966
00:48:15.925 --> 00:48:17.230
"and making a request.

967
00:48:17.255 --> 00:48:18.691
"may be granted asylum.

968
00:48:19.597 --> 00:48:21.251
I turned myself in.

969
00:48:21.276 --> 00:48:23.974
I wanted my crew to know
me for who I really was.

970
00:48:23.999 --> 00:48:26.524
"Starfleet captains
must exercise discretion

971
00:48:26.549 --> 00:48:29.422
"in judgement when
offering asylum.

972
00:48:29.453 --> 00:48:31.929
"Status is confirmed
by a Starfleet tribunal

973
00:48:31.954 --> 00:48:33.999
or designated authority."

974
00:48:37.342 --> 00:48:40.747
Fearing for their life.

975
00:48:40.935 --> 00:48:44.460
One may seek safety
within Starfleet

976
00:48:44.932 --> 00:48:47.815
and request asylum.

977
00:48:49.248 --> 00:48:51.816
Starfleet has a long tradition

978
00:48:51.841 --> 00:48:54.496
of performing rescue missions.

979
00:48:54.591 --> 00:48:56.637
How many distressed peoples

980
00:48:56.662 --> 00:48:58.838
has Starfleet aided?

981
00:48:58.863 --> 00:49:01.213
How many lives saved?

982
00:49:02.572 --> 00:49:04.444
Una Chin-Riley knew this.

983
00:49:04.487 --> 00:49:07.403
She believed in the
best of Starfleet.

984
00:49:07.428 --> 00:49:09.888
and that through it she
could find salvation

985
00:49:09.913 --> 00:49:14.570
from the hardships and
danger of her everyday life.

986
00:49:14.595 --> 00:49:16.406
Danger she faced

987
00:49:16.431 --> 00:49:19.478
just for being born an Illyrian.

988
00:49:19.730 --> 00:49:22.909
Dangers born of prejudice.

989
00:49:23.038 --> 00:49:26.737
spurred on by laws
against people like her.

990
00:49:28.243 --> 00:49:30.506
But through her hardships.

991
00:49:30.698 --> 00:49:33.265
Una saw the stars.

992
00:49:33.676 --> 00:49:36.305
She joined Starfleet
because she believed

993
00:49:36.330 --> 00:49:37.853
it was the only thing

994
00:49:37.878 --> 00:49:40.054
that could save her life.

995
00:49:40.199 --> 00:49:43.709
She fled persecution.
and within Starfleet

996
00:49:43.734 --> 00:49:45.866
she sought safety.

997
00:49:45.891 --> 00:49:48.647
And then. by turning herself in.

998
00:49:48.672 --> 00:49:50.805
Una fulfilled the third

999
00:49:50.848 --> 00:49:53.285
and final requirement
for asylum.

1000
00:49:57.681 --> 00:50:00.285
She asked for it

1001
00:50:00.496 --> 00:50:03.934
and Captain Pike granted it.

1002
00:50:03.992 --> 00:50:06.951
Like all good
Starfleet captains.

1003
00:50:06.995 --> 00:50:10.085
including Admiral
April on Perrican.

1004
00:50:10.110 --> 00:50:12.678
Na'rel and Man-us 2.

1005
00:50:12.703 --> 00:50:15.488
he exercised his judgement

1006
00:50:15.513 --> 00:50:18.081
and gave her asylum.

1007
00:50:20.068 --> 00:50:23.655
All this tribunal
needs to do now...

1008
00:50:24.692 --> 00:50:28.696
is confirm that status
to absolve them both.

1009
00:50:35.327 --> 00:50:37.982
Do you know why I love the law?

1010
00:50:38.026 --> 00:50:41.581
Because a law is not

1011
00:50:41.606 --> 00:50:44.198
a mirror to society.

1012
00:50:44.223 --> 00:50:47.444
A law is an ideal.

1013
00:50:47.621 --> 00:50:50.798
A beacon to remind us

1014
00:50:50.823 --> 00:50:53.581
how to be our better selves.

1015
00:50:53.606 --> 00:50:56.719
And you have the
opportunity today

1016
00:50:56.744 --> 00:50:59.877
to do just that.

1017
00:51:01.469 --> 00:51:04.083
Mr. Pasalk has made
this case about the law.

1018
00:51:04.108 --> 00:51:05.588
and I agree. it is.

1019
00:51:05.613 --> 00:51:09.128
By his own argument.
we cannot ignore that

1020
00:51:09.153 --> 00:51:13.036
Code 8514 is also law.

1021
00:51:13.061 --> 00:51:16.659
All I am asking you

1022
00:51:16.684 --> 00:51:19.232
to do today

1023
00:51:19.257 --> 00:51:22.175
is to be your better selves

1024
00:51:22.200 --> 00:51:24.420
and enforce the law

1025
00:51:24.463 --> 00:51:26.074
that favors my client

1026
00:51:26.117 --> 00:51:27.974
with the same dispassion

1027
00:51:27.998 --> 00:51:30.962
as the laws that
would exclude her.

1028
00:51:31.204 --> 00:51:33.249
Years ago...

1029
00:51:36.024 --> 00:51:38.461
the ideals of Starfleet

1030
00:51:38.583 --> 00:51:40.733
called a young girl

1031
00:51:40.758 --> 00:51:43.325
from the far side of
the galaxy to service.

1032
00:51:45.963 --> 00:51:48.836
Find those ideals
inside yourself.

1033
00:51:50.033 --> 00:51:51.948
Grant Una Chin-Riley

1034
00:51:51.973 --> 00:51:55.541
the asylum she was
so clearly seeking.

1035
00:52:05.330 --> 00:52:07.021
I think we
could all agree

1036
00:52:07.046 --> 00:52:09.266
that the issue of
genetic engineering

1037
00:52:09.291 --> 00:52:11.659
is a nuanced one.

1038
00:52:11.684 --> 00:52:15.819
The laws prohibiting it
exist for very good reasons.

1039
00:52:15.863 --> 00:52:18.169
And regulations must persist

1040
00:52:18.213 --> 00:52:20.693
so we may not one day
face another crisis

1041
00:52:20.737 --> 00:52:22.870
like the Eugenics Wars.

1042
00:52:22.913 --> 00:52:25.437
But this court also believes

1043
00:52:25.481 --> 00:52:29.518
that these reasons cannot
and do not allow us to treat

1044
00:52:29.543 --> 00:52:33.924
every individual
augment. Illyrian.

1045
00:52:33.968 --> 00:52:37.885
or other persons with
modified DNA the same.

1046
00:52:37.928 --> 00:52:39.843
Lines must be drawn.

1047
00:52:39.887 --> 00:52:42.977
but they must also
shift when necessary.

1048
00:52:43.020 --> 00:52:45.196
Perhaps someday Starfleet
and the Federation

1049
00:52:45.221 --> 00:52:48.348
may change its views. but today

1050
00:52:48.373 --> 00:52:50.019
I'm afraid all we
can do is consider

1051
00:52:50.044 --> 00:52:51.656
what the defense has asked.

1052
00:52:51.681 --> 00:52:53.857
That we judge the defendant's

1053
00:52:53.901 --> 00:52:56.357
specific case

1054
00:52:56.466 --> 00:53:00.383
and unique circumstances
independently.

1055
00:53:00.593 --> 00:53:02.247
And in that.

1056
00:53:02.272 --> 00:53:04.727
we grant the defendant's
request for asylum

1057
00:53:04.752 --> 00:53:07.063
and find Una Chin-Riley

1058
00:53:07.088 --> 00:53:10.656
not guilty of all charges.

1059
00:53:22.998 --> 00:53:25.217
First officer on deck.

1060
00:53:35.768 --> 00:53:38.162
- You set me up.
- How so?

1061
00:53:38.206 --> 00:53:40.556
You figured it all
out. My admission.

1062
00:53:40.599 --> 00:53:42.397
What would happen when
you put me on the stand.

1063
00:53:42.421 --> 00:53:44.423
- You knew all of it.
- No.

1064
00:53:44.448 --> 00:53:46.102
Not all of it.

1065
00:53:46.170 --> 00:53:48.800
Thank you for saving my life.

1066
00:53:48.825 --> 00:53:51.523
Hey. what are friends for?

1067
00:53:51.567 --> 00:53:53.656
Yeah.

1068
00:53:54.544 --> 00:53:57.765
I'm sorry we didn't
do more for Illyrians.

1069
00:53:57.790 --> 00:54:00.071
This was a technicality.

1070
00:54:00.181 --> 00:54:02.139
It's a start.

1071
00:54:23.226 --> 00:54:25.773
As you all know. I am not

1072
00:54:25.798 --> 00:54:27.451
the biggest fan of Starfleet.

1073
00:54:29.956 --> 00:54:33.655
But I am looking
at a starship crew

1074
00:54:33.739 --> 00:54:37.352
that proudly serves under
an Illyrian commander.

1075
00:54:39.702 --> 00:54:43.184
So. like I said...

1076
00:54:43.393 --> 00:54:45.864
it's a start.

1077
00:54:49.755 --> 00:54:51.585
Energize.

1078
00:54:56.023 --> 00:54:57.807
Hey.

1079
00:54:57.850 --> 00:55:00.679
- La'An.
- Welcome home. Chief.

1080
00:55:00.704 --> 00:55:02.706
Place wasn't the
same without you.

1081
00:55:05.162 --> 00:55:08.339
If you're all here.
who's flying the ship?

1082
00:55:08.383 --> 00:55:11.821
Oh. the thing
practically flies itself.

1083
00:55:11.864 --> 00:55:13.692
Back to your
stations. all of you.

1084
00:55:36.889 --> 00:55:38.326
Good to have you
back. Number One.

1085
00:55:38.615 --> 00:55:40.661
Good to be back. Captain.

1085
